  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi></math> of ammonium acetate solution will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "7",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>We know that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi></math> of solution of the salt made up of weak acid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and weak base <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> can be found using formula</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>log</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></mfenced></math><br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>log</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo> </mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2553</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7447</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>log</mi><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>log</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7447</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>pH</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7447</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7447</mn></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace></math></p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi></math> of salt is always <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>.<br/>Therefore, the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi></math> of given solution is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>.<br/> </p>",
